ft (freeze); timeScale: game speed, 1 normal, .25 slow motion, 0 stopped; reduceMotion: the player\n     *  asked for less motion (prefers-reduced-motion): shake and flashes are softened */\n    this.time = 0; this.real = 0; this.hitstop = 0; this.timeScale = 1; this._shakeAmt = 0; this.reduceMotion = !this.headless && !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);\n    /** camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen\n     *  rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the\n     *  focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its\n     *  top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus\n     *  sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport);\n     *  window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario\n     *  World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround)\n     *  or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps\n     *  every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min)\n     *  when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true,\n     *  edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen\n     *  pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open\n     *  ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch;\n     *  its focus keeps to bounds (world x, 