{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - User invoked `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A Stop hook blocks stopping until met.\n   - STAGE.md: build the game TASK.md describes following PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 max) using the plan's title; where they disagree, TASK.md wins; deliver everything TASK.md asks (file name, final-reply sections).\n   - TASK.md essentials: SOURCE Dragon Quest Builders; title from plan = **Dragon Quilt Builders**; deliverable `./DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521.html` (root of work folder); dev files in subfolder `DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521/`; build on my-3d2dge dist/handoff (may change engine); audio all code, Animalese/Simlish voices; AI Hub (lib/hub) multiplayer + game standalone; feature-complete vertical slice; dev mode from pause menu with live sliders + reset to defaults; attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menu, any input exits; controller-first 10-foot UI, PS glyphs default with Settings option for Xbox, keyboard/mouse native, prompts follow last input; touch-only: no touch controls, show \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract runs; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; Source Information/Testing Feedback/Engine Feedback/Prompt Feedback in chat reply AND in-game About/Credits (\"unknown\" when unconfirmable); exit-interview.json exact shape (sourceInformation {date, source, plan, genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage}, testingFeedback[4], engineFeedback[6], promptFeedback[4], aiHub {name, tagline, description, type, genre, source, series, players, controls, tags[3-6]}). Source info required: Date 2026-11-03 21:55:21; Plan file name (PLAN.md); Environment \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\"; Model \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\"; Usage only if estimates available.\n   - Testing Feedback questions: How many issues did testing catch? How many critical/game breaking? Most helpful test? Least helpful test? Engine Feedback: liked most; got stuck/guessed wrong; most important thing built yourself; hardest part; what changed in engine and why; one thing to change. Prompt Feedback: liked most; confusing; hardest; what to change.\n   - Security/process constraints (verbatim from TASK.md): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Also: \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers.\" \"Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Plan: don't clone into /tmp (full shared tmpfs).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 engine (Canvas 2D pixel renderer, `res:'ps1'` expand, depth-sorted `r.queue` with `occluder/top/box`, `_liftOrder` hook on `r._map`, x-ray silhouettes, canvas lighting `game.lights` (ambient, darkness, tint number, dark [r,g,b], refresh), Humanoid/Blob rigs, E.MOVES/E.Attack/E.Combo, E.SHAPES objects via `r.shape` (params in cache key), particles, chip audio `define/music/layer/sting`, standard pause/settings/saves (`game.saves` write/read/load/latest/show), E.Dialog not used (own Talk class), `game.script` generators, boot steps, headless `game.advance`).\n   - Custom pixel-exact views: `E.VIEWS.iso = new E.View('iso','Isometric',45,30,√2, 20/(√2·cos30·16))` (block 32x16 top, 20 px tall); threequarter pitch asin(.75), scale 1.5, zB so top/front 18 px; zoom steps iso [.75,1,1.25,1.5,2], 3/4 [2/3,1,4/3,5/3,2].\n   - Voxel world Uint8Array column-major idx=(y*W+x)*H+z; face-sprite atlas per view (yaw/pitch/scale); runs queued as occluders with exact screen `box`; lift/sink depth rules; cutaway = roof radius 6.5 + see-through slot toward camera.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world: host-authoritative, messages p/a/s/e, ≤20 msg/s, unreliable ≤1200 B; own card; ready() without key; finish({standings, scores, won, stats, awards}); time-up/end/leave/server mode; hidden-tab setInterval advance.\n   - Autopilot intent-driven AI (attract, tests, Bee bots); seeded streams DQ.rng; event bus.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder = `.../work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521/`):\n   - `engine/` (handoff copy; Playwright in engine/node_modules). Engine change: `engine/my-3d2dge.js` Humanoid accepts weapons 'needle','club','bodkin','ripper' (line ~3960 list + new drawing block before `ops.sort` in hd drawer, marked `// DQB:`).\n   - `vendor/aihub/` session.js (unmodified 1.4.0, inlined first in head), harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md.\n   - `tools/build.mjs`: node --check each src; writes root HTML (meta charset, session.js, viewport/title \"Dragon Quilt Builders\", description, hub:type Game, hub:players 1, hub:session 1, session-players 1-4, mode shared-world, minutes 8, goal, howto), boot splash, engine, `globalThis.DQ_ABOUT = <exit-interview.json or null>`, src scripts; `--release` fails without ../exit-interview.json; also dev/index.html.\n   - `tools/hub-serve.mjs`: `serve(dir)` spawns `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, parses port, `stop()` kills own PID.\n   - src modules: 00-core (DQ ns, hash/rng, Events, DQ.SCENES init, DQ.sfx forwarder, DQ.safe font-safe, DQ.store 'dqb-' keys, DQ.tuning get/set/reset, DQ.newCtx), 01-data-blocks (ids incl. 31 ruin, 32 frayedTurf, 33 darkStone, 34 knotWall unbreakable), 02-data-items (items with pixel icons, RECIPES with notion triggers, alt inputs), 03-data-objects (E.MATERIALS dq*, E.SHAPES dqBench/dqTorch/dqLantern/dqDoorLattice/dqDoorPlank (params open)/dqBed/... ; DQ.OBJECTS), 04-data-rooms, 05-data-world (regions, poi, portals, stamps ruins/shipwreck/lintCamp, patterns hall/barn1-3, demoRooms), 06-data-npcs (VOICES, NPCS, SPEAKERS), 07-data-monsters (MONSTERS, SIEGE_WAVES, SIEGE_SPAWNS), 08-data-quests (PROLOGUE, QUESTS M1–M14, S1–S3, LINES), 09b-data-tuning (23 sliders), 10-voxel-world, 11-voxel-render (patterns, Atlas, VoxelRenderer, isCut with slot, DQ.blockIcon), 12-worldgen (DQ.generateWorld, DQ.WG, DQ.stampTownRooms), 13-physics (VoxelBody), 14-input (Controls PLAY/MENU presets incl. ok/back/alt/alt2/tabPrev/tabNext/pgUp/pgDn, intent with hotStep/hotSlot, Glyphs draw/text/measure/plain/family), 15-builder, 16-inventory, 17-crafting, 18-objects, 19-rooms (+ leak hint toast), 20-town, 21-nav (Nav A*, Walker), 22-npcs, 23-monsters, 24-combat (+Drops), 25-siege (+BallistaCtl), 26-bosses (ButtonBrain, GnarlBrain, rings, cutscenes buttonsworthIntro/gnarlgrimEnter), 27-time (Clock), 28-story (Talk, Quests, QuestHooks, Interact, Cutscenes C.*), 28b-beats (DQ.Beats apply/_apply/stitchRift; ctx.quiet during apply), 29-ui-hud (Icons, Hud + static panel/heart/balloon/speech/pins/fuzz/portrait), 30-ui-menus (UI stack, Satchel, Craft, Chest, Travel, BannerScreen, DQ.Menus), 31-audio (SONGS 14, JINGLES 13, SFX ~60, AudioX with voice synth & director), 32-save (DQ.Save write/apply/migrate/tick/autosave/checkpoint/restoreCheckpoint), 33-dev (DevScreen tabs Cheats/Warp/Spawn/Story/Tuning/Debug/World, DQ.Dev open/persist/restore/warp/completeStep/exportStamp/importStamp/drawOverlays), 34-attract (DQ.Attract.anyInput, VIGNETTES 9, scene attract with autoTalk 1.1), 35-ai (Autopilot: intent, run, walkTo, standNear, reach, breakAt (fail fast, collect), collect, select, placeAt (timeout 6, detailed fail reasons), buildStamp, craft, talk, readTalk (autoTalk), readDialog, fight, manBallista), 36-net (Net: host broadcasts all edits via events, left set, builderFor, applyOp/applyEvent, puppet monsters), 37-bee (DQ.Bee gen/makeCtx/demo, Round, scene bee with card/countdown/play/ended, supports ctx.driver), 38-scenes (Play.make/wire/useKey/onKO/update/camera/placing/cutaway/explore/draw/blockLights/frayvern; ListMenu; DQ.demoCtx; scenes title/newgame/intro/play/results/credits/about; DQ.Title.logo; DQ.touchOnly), 99-main (DQ.SETTINGS incl. glyphs override default 'playstation', camView, difficulty, autoHop, sprintMode, textSpeed, tracker, tutorials, cutaway, voices; Game with menu items Satchel/Dev Tools/About & Credits; saves write/read; keydown tracking; game.debug snapshot/teleport/give/flag/beat; deep link `#play[:beat]`, `#bee`, `#attract`, `#about`; boot steps).\n   - Key recent code (28b-beats.js) — clearing demo room footprints:\n     ```js\n     if (stage && !ctx.flags['stamp_' + stage]) { const order = ['lv2','lv3','lv4']; for (const rm of DQ.WORLD.demoRooms) if (order.indexOf(rm.beat) <= order.indexOf(stage)) for (let y = rm.y; y < rm.y + rm.d; y++) for (let x = rm.x; x < rm.x + rm.w; x++) for (let z = 8; z < 13; z++) { const o = ctx.objects.at(x, y, z); if (o && !o.def.banner && !o.def.portal) ctx.objects.remove(o, { silent: true }); }\n       const objs = DQ.stampTownRooms(w, [], stage); ...\n     b.bag.add('bun', 3); if (idx >= 1) b.bag.remove('banner', b.bag.count('banner')); if (idx >= 5) b.bag.remove('hallPattern', b.bag.count('hallPattern'));\n     ```\n   - Tests: `tests/run.mjs` (prints only failures + \"N passed, M failed (s)\"; --only, --browser), `tests/lib/load.mjs`, `tests/unit/core.test.mjs`, `tests/play/playthrough.test.mjs` (Autopilot full chapter, `PT_UNTIL=M4|S1`), `tests/play/systems.test.mjs`, `tests/net/fakehub.mjs` + `net.test.mjs`, `tests/browser/hub.test.mjs`, `tests/browser/input.test.mjs`; `tests/browser/shots.mjs` and `shot.mjs` (screenshots to check-output; set `process.env.TMPDIR` to check-output/tmp; launch with `--disable-dev-shm-usage`).\n   - `DEVLOG.md`: API notes + progress log.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Load-order: DQ.CUTSCENES and DQ.SCENES used before defined → `DQ.CUTSCENES = DQ.CUTSCENES || {}` in 26/28; `DQ.SCENES` initialized in core.\n   - `I.down('Mouse2')` unknown action → `I.held.has('Mouse2')`.\n   - Wake cutscene dark overlay drawn over dialog → fades overlay moved before HUD/talk/ui (and a misplaced closing brace fixed).\n   - Beats triggered cutscenes/popups → `ctx.quiet` (Cutscenes.play applies, crafting.learn silent, Hud toast/popup/banner skip).\n   - Builder hidden in Lint Hollow: engine x-ray mask uses 120px guess box → pass exact `box` per run; cutaway extended with see-through slot toward camera (k ≤ 16, `t-1 >= L + kk*ds/zh`, slotW 3.2, slotLen).\n   - Lighting API misuse (tint is number) → ambient/darkness/tint .4/dark arrays + refresh.\n   - Stair ramp evaluated at clamp point → leading edge `_stairTop(x,y,z,px,py,rr)`.\n   - Walker.steer infinite recursion (A* every frame, stack overflow, 80x slow) → iterative node skipping, end-of-partial-path arrives, repath timer.\n   - `quests.wire()` never called → called in Play.make.\n   - Drops out of pickup range for AI → Autopilot.collect after breakAt; magnet 2 blocks.\n   - brkFar invalidated by cutaway → only reach matters.\n   - AI blocked by modal dialog → Autopilot autoTalk + `Play.update` calls `o.ai.readTalk()`; drivers pass `ai`.\n   - AI standing on wall tops → standNear penalties.\n   - Bubble collected forever (fly=0 falsy) → `bb.fly = 1e-6`.\n   - Door state check used tween `open` → `isOpen`.\n   - touchOnly navigator ReferenceError in Node → guarded.\n   - Bee poi.tunnelMark undefined → guarded.\n   - Net: host edits not broadcast → host listens to blockPlaced/Broken/objectPlaced/Removed/Broken (skip by 'net'); leaver re-created by late packet → `left` set.\n   - /tmp full (shared) → TMPDIR=check-output/tmp for Chromium.\n   - Demo rooms furniture blocked by wild plants → Beats clears footprints.\n   - Many test-script fixes (branches/lint/logs gathering, Hall site moved to (66..76,58..66), ballista with line of sight, Hall retry).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Current status: all headless suites pass (287 checks: core 58, playthrough 88, systems ~73, net 68); browser hub harness 6/6 (all 4 hub scenarios + standalone title); browser input 13/13; engine check.mjs no errors (draw ~20 ms iso). Visual review done for title, hollow, town, bag, map, craft, boss, night, spire, beeplay, newgame, attract, tq; HUD fixes applied (gated Cheer badge, non-modal dialog at top y=62, Bee HUD offset, hide town badge in bee, pattern panel auto width, Satchel tab glyph position, context-aware bag action row).\n   - Not yet re-run after the last changes (leak hint in rooms commit, Beats footprint clearing/key removal) — need to rerun `node tests/run.mjs`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The `/goal` command text (quoted in section 1). No other user messages besides system/hook reminders (\"say in a few words what you're doing\" nudges).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Rerun `node tests/run.mjs` (and `--browser`) after latest edits; fix any failures.\n   - Optionally review remaining screenshots (siege, about, dev, intro, rot, quarry, tweed, coast, fraying).\n   - Write `../exit-interview.json` (work folder root, beside the HTML) with exact shape, ASCII-friendly text; validate with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n   - Final `node tools/build.mjs --release` (embeds DQ_ABOUT for About screen); verify About pages show the data (systems test checks About when DQ_ABOUT present); grep src for TODO/FIXME/placeholder.\n   - Final chat reply containing Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback sections (same text as exit interview).\n   - Suggested exit-interview content: sourceInformation date \"2026-11-03 21:55:21\", source \"Dragon Quest Builders\", plan \"PLAN.md\", genre \"Sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building)\", perspective \"Isometric 2.5D third person, rotatable in 90-degree steps, zoom steps; optional three-quarter view\", tech \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (Canvas 2D, full engine, one modified file), own voxel world/renderer, Web Audio, AI Hub Session client 1.4.0, Node 24 vm headless tests, Playwright 1.63.0\", art \"engine native pixel style; patchwork-quilt voxel textures with stitched seams, E.SHAPES furniture, HD Humanoid/Blob rigs\", animation \"engine procedural rigs, E.MOVES plus new moves place/eat/stir/crank/hammer, poses, tweens/scripts\", audio \"14 original chip songs on a leitmotif, 13 jingles, ~60 code sfx, Animalese formant voices per speaker, Voices volume\", online \"AI Hub shared-world Quilting Bee 1-4 players (own card, host snapshots, server mode); solo Bee with bots\", testing \"headless vm suites via game.advance/game.debug incl. full scripted playthrough; Playwright hub harness 4 scenarios, input test, screenshots\", research \"none beyond reading the engine handoff (API.md, renderer/Body/Dialog/Input source) and AI Hub README/harness; no web research\", environment \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", model \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\", usage \"unknown\" (session time ~2.5+ h from 21:55). aiHub: name \"Dragon Quilt Builders\", tagline \"Stitch a frayed world back together\", description per plan, type \"Game\", genre \"RPG\", source \"Dragon Quest Builders\", series \"Dragon Quest\", players \"1–4\", controls \"Stick/WASD move · ✕/Space jump · □/Click break · △/Right-click place · L1 R1/wheel items · ○/F talk\", tags [\"building\",\"crafting\",\"co-op\",\"fantasy\",\"comedy\",\"pixel art\"].\n   - Testing feedback facts: issues caught ~20 (Walker recursion, quest wiring, infinite Cheer bubble, host edits not broadcast, leaver recreated, door state, stair ramp, cutaway/x-ray hiding hero, AI dialog block, demo rooms furniture, touchOnly guard, Bee poi guard, etc.); critical ~5 (Walker freeze, quests.wire, infinite cheer, net desync, hidden hero); most helpful: scripted playthrough; least helpful: early pickScreen/stairs unit checks with wrong expectations (or the core room matrix). Engine feedback: liked rigs/shapes/headless advance; guessed wrong on x-ray box heuristic and lighting tint type; built voxel world/renderer/physics/nav; hardest: depth sorting/x-ray in voxel world; changed: Humanoid sewing weapons; one change: engine-native voxel/multi-level map support or occluder box API.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary, I fixed the Lv4 beat's demo rooms (plants blocked furniture) by clearing objects in each demo room footprint before `DQ.stampTownRooms`, and removed leftover key items (banner, hallPattern) in Beats. Verification output: all seven demo rooms detected with correct types (\"bedroom, workshop, guardPost, messHall, kitchen, smithy, bedroom2 → bedroom\"). Also had just added a room leak-hint toast in `Rooms.commit` (src/19-rooms.js). tests/lib/dbg.mjs deleted.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Rerun the full test command after these edits (`node tests/run.mjs`, then `node tests/run.mjs --browser`), fix any failures, then write `exit-interview.json` in the work r