{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQEMDBavGzZCPYF8ZecvjK","type":"tool_result","content":"69 passed, 0 failed (8.4 s)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9acc64b9-af41-4198-9bbd-536ec13fbed1","uuid":"f5a022f2-a577-40b9-93f6-aeb048457212","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:24:58.043Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"69 passed, 0 failed (8.4 s)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1343,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1343,"newLines":10,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghVDEed8f4roXVmxG8pe\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1380,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":712776,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1380},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"94b6f61d-3425-4074-a554-09e41423f140\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:23:48.212Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghVDEGZ9BUMQy4ye8hYr\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":9620,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghVDEed8f4roXVmxG8pe\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've built **Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball** and saved it as one HTML file in this folder, with `exit-interview.json` beside it (it parses and every field is filled). The test command passes all 230 checks, including the AI Hub harness in all four of its scenarios and a browser run from `file://` with no console errors.\\n\\n**What's in it**\\n- **2v2 beach volleyball:** one Play button with a timing ring for bump, set, spike and serve, plus dive, shot/block and Mine/Yours calls. It has all the faults and rally scoring, two cameras, Sonny's commentary, a crowd, celebrations and highlight replays.\\n- **Five-day vacation:**\\n  - five walkable places on an island map: the courts, the pool, the Promenade, your villa and the casino at night;\\n  - weather, moods and NPC teams, plus chats, gifts, team-ups and partners who walk out on you;\\n  - three shops with 21 swimsuits you can try on, a wardrobe and a journal;\\n  - the story: tutorial, events, semifinal, a final against Sonny & Pepper with special rules, a farewell party, two endings, credits, results and New Vacation+.\\n- **Minigames:** Pool Hop, a rhythm game played on the music's beat, and a casino with cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette.\\n- **Postcards:** a photo mode and an album; you can set a postcard as the title backdrop.\\n- **Saves:** three slots, an autosave and Continue.\\n- **Multiplayer:** Beach Match for 1–4 players on one machine (pads or a split keyboard), and AI Hub shared-world online play with the game's own card.\\n- **Attract mode, Dev Mode and UI:** the attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title or menu, and any input exits it. Dev Mode opens from the pause menu, with tools and live sliders that reset to defaults. The UI is controller-first: PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option in Settings, native keyboard and mouse, and a \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" screen on touch-only devices.\\n- **Audio:** all made in code — 9 songs, jingles, sound effects and gibberish voices for each character.\\n\\n**Where I cut back from the plan**\\n- No motion-capture clips. Every move uses the engine's own animation with arm IK on top.\\n- Postcards are stored as small saved pictures rather than scenes rebuilt live.\\n- The island map is a tile map with pins, not the plan's full set of landmarks.\\n- AI rallies average a reasonable length but can still run to about 20 touches.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 23:11:45\\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball (Team Ninja / Tecmo, Xbox, 2003)\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:**\\n  - Genre: sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim vacation and minigames (rhythm Pool Hop, casino).\\n  - Matches: a side-on TV Broadcast camera, with a Serve Cam behind your team as the alternative.\\n  - Places: three-quarter view. Island map: isometric. Shops, casino tables and menus: full-screen canvas UI over the world.\\n- **Tech:**\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine, with six changes) and plain JavaScript in one IIFE.\\n  - AI Hub session client 1.4.0, unmodified.\\n  - Tests ran on Node 24 with Playwright 1.63.0 and Chromium.\\n  - One self-contained HTML file with no runtime libraries or network.\\n- **Art Direction:**\\n  - The engine's native PS1-era pixel art.\\n  - HD rigs on a custom athletic build, with code-drawn swimsuit cuts, 14 patterns, extra hair styles and accessories.\\n  - Resort objects as engine shape data, backdrops for each time of day, and a tropical palette.\\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs, plus an arm-IK layer for every volleyball move, celebration, emote and photo pose. Moves are timed from the match's contact plan.\\n- **Audio:**\\n  - 9 songs on the engine's sequencer, with added instruments: steel drum, marimba, pluck, bell, organ, pad.\\n  - 10 jingles, about 50 sound effects and ambience loops.\\n  - Animalese-style voices spoken letter by letter, with a voice profile per character.\\n- **Online:**\\n  - AI Hub Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\\n  - The host runs the match; every copy flies the ball from the same launches on the hub clock.\\n  - Each player's touches are judged on their own copy and checked by the host.\\n  - CPUs fill empty seats, and the host reports the result with standings, stats and an MVP.\\n- **Testing:** 14 suites behind one command (`node test/run.mjs`, which prints only failures and a count; 230 checks):\\n  - headless suites driving the game through its debug handle, plus a scripted whole-vacation playthrough to both endings;\\n  - a Playwright browser tour, including a touch-only device;\\n  - the AI Hub harness in four scenarios;\\n  - screenshots and the engine's checker for looks;\\n  - no subagents.\\n- **Research:** read the engine handoff (API card, index, guide sections, asset card, the sports kit, and the source for the rig, Dialog and audio) and the AI Hub README and harness. The source game was described from general knowledge; no web research.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 25 game issues:\\n   - two crashes, one from a name clash and one from a variable scoping slip;\\n   - a scene drawn before it was set up, and a sound table the browser rejected;\\n   - an attract mode you couldn't leave during its photo beat;\\n   - 50-touch rallies, and AI skill that barely changed results;\\n   - a slot machine paying out 132%;\\n   - a key clash on the split-keyboard join screen;\\n   - missing font characters, plus framing and overlap problems on several screens.\\n2. **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** About 6:\\n   - a crash on the title (two systems both named `G.dev`);\\n   - a crash on every attack;\\n   - the scene list missing at load;\\n   - the menu crashing when drawn before it was set up;\\n   - the music instrument error;\\n   - the attract mode trapping the player.\\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted whole-vacation playthrough (both endings, every story event, casino, Pool Hop, saves) together with the AI-vs-AI match statistics. For online play, the AI Hub harness in four scenarios.\\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Single-frame title screenshots and the engine checker's view cycling. Each was useful once, but neither shows timing or motion, which only the scripted runs caught.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The character rig. One constructor gives a shaded, dressed, animated character that also draws its own portrait, and its pose can be adjusted afterwards. So swimsuits, new hair and every volleyball move were additions, not rewrites. The fixed-step clock made every test repeatable.\\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** A little. I passed 0 as a ring's transparency, used a material pattern name that doesn't exist (`plaster`), and had to read the source to learn how joined players inherit split-keyboard keys. The index answered most other questions.\\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The volleyball itself: the ball's flight, contact planning, the timing judge, blocks, faults, and the AI and its error model. Also the swimsuit cuts and patterns drawn on the torso.\\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Hooking into the character's drawing, which is one large function. Swimsuits needed an engine change to add a callback.\\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Six changes, each marked `AOA:` in the source and listed in ENGINE-CHANGES.md:\\n   - PlayStation symbols and stepper arrows added to the pixel font;\\n   - a Button symbols setting: PlayStation by default, Xbox as the option;\\n   - a per-letter voice hook in the dialog box, for the gibberish voices;\\n   - a separate voice volume, plus new instrument sounds for the music;\\n   - swim shorts and a swimsuit-drawing hook on the character rig;\\n   - Options ignored while Create is held, an AI Hub rule.\\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented drawing hook for each body part, so new clothing needs no engine edit.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** It is concrete about the player's experience (10-foot controller-first UI, glyph rules, the touch-only screen, attract mode, dev sliders) and about the deliverables, so it's clear when the work is done.\\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan asks for far more content than one medium-effort session can fully build, and how to trade breadth for depth was left to judgement.\\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting a five-day vacation sim, three minigames and online play around a timing-based sports game, with every screen controller-first.\\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Say which parts of the plan are musts and which are stretch goals, so the builder can scope deliberately.\\n\\nFiles are in this folder:\\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145.html\\n- exit-interview.json\\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/ — dev folder with the source, tests, README-DEV.md and ENGINE-CHANGES.md\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1380,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":712776,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1380},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"59309b2c-47c6-4c07-a42b-bc9f06ff5d04\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:24:09.278Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghVDEGZ9BUMQy4ye8hYr\"}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The html and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply has the four sections. But the transcript admits gaps against TASK.md's 'every feature implemented' requirement: the final reply itself says the island map is 'a tile map with pins, not the plan's full set of landmarks' and that AI rallies 'can still run to about 20 touches'. Postcards are saved as pictures rather than specs, and the plan's motion-capture clips were not used. The 'no placeholders or stubs' check is also unverified: the test that greps src/ for TODO/TBD/placeholder only ran as part of the suite, and the source was never checked for stubbed features against the full feature list. The condition's requirement that every feature in TASK.md is implemented is not clearly met by the transcript evidence.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"9a0e2c22-4cdc-4ba2-944b-c56aa4778638\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:24:31.293Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"9e8fe31e-71c9-4749-8244-8b6853ef3570\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",