lighting tint as a colour (it is a number). The engine map is a height field, so a multi-level voxel world needed its own renderer. I also used an input name that is not an action (Mouse2) before checking the held set.\",\n    \"The voxel world: storage, a face-sprite atlas per view, a renderer that merges block runs into depth-sorted occluders with cutaway and a see-through slot toward the camera, voxel physics and A* navigation. After that, room detection and the AI pilot that drives the attract mode, the tests and the Bee bots.\",\n    \"Depth sorting voxel runs against the engine's sprites in its painter-sorted queue (occluder, top and box rules, the lift order hook), with x-ray, at two view angles and four camera turns.\",\n    \"One file, my-3d2dge.js: the Humanoid rig now accepts four more held items (a darning needle, a cobble club, a copper bodkin and a seam ripper) drawn in its HD drawer, because the source's weapons are also its building tools and the rig's weapon list is closed. Nothing else in the engine was changed.\",\n    \"First-class multi-level or voxel map support in the renderer, or at least an occluder API that takes exact screen boxes, so a block-building game does not need its own renderer.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"It is concrete about what done means: the file names, one test command that prints only failures, the exit interview shape, the final reply sections, and a clear rule that TASK.md wins over the plan. The freedom to change the engine, and an AI Hub spec with a harness to test against, made the multiplayer verifiable.\",\n    \"The plan names a different deliverable file (a max-effort name from another run) than TASK.md does; TASK.md wins, but it is easy to get wrong. The Source Information field Testing asks for the testing parameters allowed, which reads two ways (the rules, or what was run). Usage asks for cost and token numbers the agent cannot see.\",\n    \"The scope: a feature-complete vertical slice of a voxel building RPG (building, rooms, residents, combat, a siege, bosses, a story chapter, multiplayer, attract mode, dev tools) on a 2D engine with no voxel support, while checking the visuals only through screenshots.\",\n    \"Make the plan's deliverable name match TASK.md, give the agent a way to read its own token and cost usage or drop that field, and say whether Testing should list the rules or the tests run.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Dragon Quilt Builders\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Stitch a frayed world back together\",\n    \"description\": \"The dragon Frayvern pulled out the Golden Thread and swallowed everyone's knack for making things, and you are the last Builder. Break and place blocks, craft from Notions, build rooms that residents move into, raise the town of Thimbleton, defend it in a siege and unpick the knotted boss Gnarlgrim, or build a Quilt Barn together in a co-op Quilting Bee round.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"RPG\",\n    \"source\": \"Dragon Quest Builders\",\n    \"series\": \"Dragon Quest\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Left stick or WASD move, Cross or Space jump, Square or left click swing and break, Triangle or right click place, L1 and R1 or the mouse wheel pick items, Circle or F talk, Q and E or the right stick turn the camera\",\n    \"tags\": [\"building\", \"crafting\", \"co-op\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018ef2Mm75SSbG1oq7zrK59L","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
