{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghXAfsq16EMn9sCHFGeB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FAr1uUAd9nVqFfEkfukQVq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> DEVLOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Issues found (the exit interview's counts come from this list; * = critical / game-breaking)\nCaught by the scripted tests (headless suites, network suite, browser checks): 21\n1. * Module load order: DQ.CUTSCENES / DQ.SCENES used before they were defined (the game did not boot)\n2. 'Mouse2' read as an action name (it is a held code)\n3. The wake cutscene's dark overlay drawn over its own dialog\n4. Story-beat setup firing cutscenes and popups (now ctx.quiet)\n5. * The Builder hidden behind tall voxel runs (engine x-ray guessed a 120 px box; runs now pass an exact box) and the Hollow rim (cutaway slot)\n6. Lighting set with a colour where the engine takes a number (tint) and arrays (dark)\n7. Stair ramps evaluated at the clamp point instead of the leading edge\n8. * Walker.steer recursing (A* every frame): stack overflow and an 80x slowdown\n9. * quests.wire() never called: the story could not advance\n10. Drops landing out of the AI's pickup range\n11. Cutaway invalidating explicit break targets\n12. The AI blocked by an open modal dialog\n13. The AI standing on wall tops\n14. * A Cheer bubble collectable forever (fly = 0 read as false)\n15. Door state read from the tween instead of isOpen\n16. touchOnly reading navigator in Node\n17. The Bee reading an undefined poi.tunnelMark\n18. * The host's own edits never broadcast (multiplayer desync)\n19. A player who left re-created by a late packet\n20. Demo rooms' furniture blocked by wild plants after a story-beat jump\n21. * Optional cutscene apply: a quiet quest completion still called apply directly (boot error), caught by the next run\nCaught by screenshot review: 14\n22. Cheer badge shown before it means anything   23. Non-modal dialog over the HUD   24. Bee HUD offset   25. Town badge in the Bee\n26. Pattern panel width   27. Satchel tab glyph position   28. Bag action row not following the selection\n29. Quest tracker covering the health bar   30. Siege banner bar label cramped   31. Used-up Heartpatch left on the hotbar\n32. Dev Tools title under the corner buttons   33. Prologue prompt row clipped   34. About tabs past the right edge\n35. Tuning rows without slider tracks\nFound by reading code after a screenshot: 1\n36. Enter (OK and Start on a keyboard) both turned and skipped the prologue pages (now a browser check)\nFound by the stub scans (TODO words, empty bodies, unused values): 4\n37. The Bee's crafted() hook did nothing and clients never sent their crafts (now a network check)\n38. The Builder's landing squash was set but never drawn (now the rig's land() and a jump stretch)\n39. Skipped cutscenes left the training dummy, a scripted resident, or no arrival / skill note (now a systems check)\n40. Dev rows whose OK action was empty (OK now steps the value)\nTotal 40; critical 7 (1, 5, 8, 9, 14, 18, 21).\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; j=json.load(open(p))\nj['testingFeedback'][0]=\"40, listed in DEVLOG.md: 21 caught by the scripted tests (headless suites, the network suite and the browser checks), 14 by screenshot review (HUD panels overlapping, the quest tracker covering the health bar, clipped prompt rows, tabs past the screen edge), 1 by reading code after a screenshot (Enter both turning and skipping the prologue), and 4 by scans for stubs (a Bee scoring hook that did nothing, a landing squash never drawn, cutscene skips that left a training dummy or skipped a note, Dev rows with empty actions).\"\nj['testingFeedback'][1]=\"7: the game failing to boot from a module load-order error, the residents' path walker recursing until the stack overflowed (a freeze), the quest system never being wired so the story could not advance, a Cheer bubble that could be collected forever, the host's own edits never reaching other players (a desync in multiplayer), the Builder hidden behind walls in the first region by the x-ray and cutaway, and a late regression where a quiet quest completion broke the boot (caught by the next test run).\"\nj['sourceInformation']['testing']=j['sourceInformation']['testing'].replace('309 checks pass','311 checks pass')\nj['sourceInformation']['usage']=\"Cost unknown; tokens unknown; session time about 3 hours (2026-11-03 21:55 to about 2026-11-04 00:55, wall clock)\"\njson.dump(j,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2); open(p,'a').write('\\n')\nEOF\ngrep -c \"311 checks\" ../exit-interview.json; date +%H:%M","description":"Log the issue list and update the interview counts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":174232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":585},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9acc64b9-af41-4198-9bbd-536ec13fbed1","uuid":"e0c043e1-30f3-4837-94bf-f3f12be8ce10","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:49:45.421Z","request_id":"req_011CghXAfbhk3ouyWnn8v3eK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FAr1uUAd9nVqFfEkfukQVq":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521 && cat >> DEVLOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Issues found (the exit interview's counts come from this list; * = critical / game-breaking)\nCaught by the scripted tests (headless suites, network suite, browser checks): 21\n1. * Module load order: DQ.CUTSCENES / DQ.SCENES used before they were defined (the game did not boot)\n2. 'Mouse2' read as an action name (it is a held code)\n3. The wa