.wire() never called: the story could not advance","+10. Drops landing out of the AI's pickup range","+11. Cutaway invalidating explicit break targets","+12. The AI blocked by an open modal dialog","+13. The AI standing on wall tops","+14. * A Cheer bubble collectable forever (fly = 0 read as false)","+15. Door state read from the tween instead of isOpen","+16. touchOnly reading navigator in Node","+17. The Bee reading an undefined poi.tunnelMark","+18. * The host's own edits never broadcast (multiplayer desync)","+19. A player who left re-created by a late packet","+20. Demo rooms' furniture blocked by wild plants after a story-beat jump","+21. * Optional cutscene apply: a quiet quest completion still called apply directly (boot error), caught by the next run","+Caught by screenshot review: 14","+22. Cheer badge shown before it means anything   23. Non-modal dialog over the HUD   24. Bee HUD offset   25. Town badge in the Bee","+26. Pattern panel width   27. Satchel tab glyph position   28. Bag action row not following the selection","+29. Quest tracker covering the health bar   30. Siege banner bar label cramped   31. Used-up Heartpatch left on the hotbar","+32. Dev Tools title under the corner buttons   33. Prologue prompt row clipped   34. About tabs past the right edge","+35. Tuning rows without slider tracks","+Found by reading code after a screenshot: 1","+36. Enter (OK and Start on a keyboard) both turned and skipped the prologue pages (now a browser check)","+Found by the stub scans (TODO words, empty bodies, unused values): 4","+37. The Bee's crafted() hook did nothing and clients never sent their crafts (now a network check)","+38. The Builder's landing squash was set but never drawn (now the rig's land() and a jump stretch)","+39. Skipped cutscenes left the training dummy, a scripted resident, or no arrival / skill note (now a systems check)","+40. Dev rows whose OK action was empty (OK now steps the value)","+Total 40; critical 7 (1, 5, 8, 9, 14, 18, 21)."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/exit-interview.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":15,"newStart":10,"newLines":15,"lines":["     \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural rigs and move library (E.MOVES, attacks and combos) plus new moves for placing, eating, stirring, cranking the ballista and hammering at stations, poses and tweens for cutscenes, particles for Cheer bubbles, glints, stitches and fraying\",","     \"audio\": \"All code, no audio files: 14 original chip songs built on one leitmotif, 13 jingles (Notion, room, level up and more), 39 synthesized sound effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices with a pitch and timbre per speaker (10 voices), a music director that follows place, time of day and danger, and a separate Voices volume\",","     \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world Quilting Bee round for 1-4 players: host-authoritative world edits and snapshots, the game's own card, ready without a key press, standings and finish, leave, time-up, end and server mode; playable solo from the title with bot helpers; the story game is single-player and unchanged outside a session\",","-    \"testing\": \"Allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state (game.advance and game.debug), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Used: node tests/run.mjs (unit, systems, full Chapter One playthrough by an AI pilot, a fake-hub network suite with 2 and 4 copies, latency and loss, server mode) and --browser (the AI Hub harness 4 scenarios plus standalone, real keyboard and mouse input in Chromium); 309 checks pass\",","+    \"testing\": \"Allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state (game.advance and game.debug), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Used: node tests/run.mjs (unit, systems, full Chapter One playthrough by an AI pilot, a fake-hub network suite with 2 and 4 copies, latency and loss, server mode) and --browser (the AI Hub harness 4 scenarios plus standalone, real keyboard and mouse input in Chromium); 311 checks pass\",","     \"research\": \"None on the web. Read the engine handoff (API notes and the renderer, body, input and dialog source) and the AI Hub lib/hub README, session.js and harness\",","     \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",","     \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\",","-    \"usage\": \"Cost unknown; tokens unknown; session time about 2 hours 45 minutes (2026-11-03 21:55 to about 2026-11-04 00:42, wall clock)\"","+    \"usage\": \"Cost unknown; tokens unknown; session time about 3 hours (2026-11-03 21:55 to about 2026-11-04 00:55, wall clock)\"","   },","   \"testingFeedback\": [","-    \"About 34. Roughly 20 were caught by the scripted tests (headless suites, the network suite and the browser checks), about 13 by screenshot review (HUD panels overlapping, a clipped prompt row, the quest tracker covering the health bar, the Dev Tools title under the corner buttons), and 1 by the scan for stubs (a Bee scoring hook that did nothing and a craft message that was never sent).\",","-    \"6: the game failing to boot from a module load-order error, the residents' path walker recursing until the stack overflowed (a freeze), the quest system never being wired so the story could not advance, a Cheer bubble that could be collected forever, the host's own edits never reaching other players (a desync in multiplayer), and the Builder hidden behind walls in the first region by the x-ray and cutaway. A seventh was close: Enter both turned and skipped the prologue pages.\",","+    \"40, listed in DEVLOG.md: 21 caught by the scripted tests (headless suites, the network suite and the browser checks), 14 by screenshot review (HUD panels overlapping, the quest tracker covering the health bar, clipped prompt rows, tabs past the screen edge), 1 by reading code after a screenshot (Enter both turning and skipping the prologue), and 4 by scans for stubs (a Bee scoring hook that did nothing, a landing squash never drawn, cutscene skips that left a training dummy or skipped a note, Dev rows with empty actions).\",","+    \"7: the game failing to boot from a module load-order error, the residents' path walker recursing until the stack overflowed (a freeze), the quest system never being wired so the story could not advance, a Cheer bubble that could be collected forever, the host's own edits never reaching other players (a desync in multiplayer), the Builder hidden behind walls in the first region by the x-ray and cutaway, and a late regression where a quiet quest completion broke the boot (caught by the next test run).\",","     \"The scripted playthrough: an AI pilot plays Chapter One from the first quest to the credits and the side quests through the same input intents a player uses. It found the unwired quests, the path walker freeze, room detection gaps, dialogs blocking play, and story beats that left furniture blocked by plants.\",","     \"Early unit checks of screen picking and stair heights: their failures were mostly wrong expectations in the tests themselves, not bugs in the game, and the playthrough covered the same code better.\"","   ],"]},{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":6,"newStart":46,"newLines":13,"lines":["     \"series\": \"Dragon Quest\",","     \"players\": \"1–4\",","     \"controls\": \"Left stick or WASD move, Cross or Space jump, Square or left click swing and break, Triangle or right click place, L1 and R1 or the mouse wheel pick items, Circle or F talk, Q and E or the right stick turn the camera\",","-    \"tags\": [\"building\", \"crafting\", \"co-op\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]","+    \"tags\": [","+      \"building\",","+      \"crafting\",","+      \"co-op\",","+      \"fantasy\",","+      \"comedy\",","+      \"pixel art\"","+    ]","   }"," }"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521/DEVLOG.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/exit-interview.json"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FAr1uUAd9nVqFfEkfukQVq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
