 mouse input in Chromium); 356 checks pass, including a TASK.md requirements suite and a content audit (REQUIREMENTS.md maps each TASK.md line to its checks)\\n01:14\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"bashEditDiff\":{\"files\":[{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521/DEVLOG.md\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":72,\"oldLines\":4,\"newStart\":72,\"newLines\":11,\"lines\":[\" 38. The Builder's landing squash was set but never drawn (now the rig's land() and a jump stretch)\",\" 39. Skipped cutscenes left the training dummy, a scripted resident, or no arrival / skill note (now a systems check)\",\" 40. Dev rows whose OK action was empty (OK now steps the value)\",\"-Total 40; critical 7 (1, 5, 8, 9, 14, 18, 21).\",\"+Found by the content audit (tests/unit/requirements.test.mjs: everything defined must be reachable and used): 3\",\"+41. The Golden Thimble (a side-quest reward) did nothing though it promised courage: now +2 attack while carried\",\"+42. The 'undone' jingle was never played: now plays when the Builder comes undone in the story\",\"+43. The rock decoration was defined but never placed: now scattered on the Crags and the Coast (own RNG stream)\",\"+Total 43; critical 7 (1, 5, 8, 9, 14, 18, 21).\",\"+Test-script fixes (not game bugs), made when the rocks changed the world: gatherPlant skips a target it already tried;\",\"+M3 gathers its own Lint before the torch; the boss fight's fallback ballista searches for a free cell with a clear line.\",\"+REQUIREMENTS.md maps every TASK.md line to the checks that verify it.\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/exit-interview.json\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":10,\"oldLines\":16,\"newStart\":10,\"newLines\":16,\"lines\":[\"     \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine's procedural rigs and move library (E.MOVES, attacks and combos) plus new moves for placing, eating, stirring, cranking the ballista and hammering at stations, poses and tweens for cutscenes, particles for Cheer bubbles, glints, stitches and fraying\\\",\",\"     \\\"audio\\\": \\\"All code, no audio files: 14 original chip songs built on one leitmotif, 13 jingles (Notion, room, level up and more), 39 synthesized sound effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices with a pitch and timbre per speaker (10 voices), a music director that follows place, time of day and danger, and a separate Voices volume\\\",\",\"     \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world Quilting Bee round for 1-4 players: host-authoritative world edits and snapshots, the game's own card, ready without a key press, standings and finish, leave, time-up, end and server mode; playable solo from the title with bot helpers; the story game is single-player and unchanged outside a session\\\",\",\"-    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state (game.advance and game.debug), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Used: node tests/run.mjs (unit, systems, full Chapter One playthrough by an AI pilot, a fake-hub network suite with 2 and 4 copies, latency and loss, server mode) and --browser (the AI Hub harness 4 scenarios plus standalone, real keyboard and mouse input in Chromium); 312 checks pass\\\",\",\"+    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Allowed: headless scripts that play the game and check its state (game.advance and game.debug), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Used: node tests/run.mjs (unit, systems, full Chapter One playthrough by an AI pilot, a fake-hub network suite with 2 and 4 copies, latency and loss, server mode) and --browser (the AI Hub harness 4 scenarios plus standalone, real keyboard and mouse input in Chromium); 356 checks pass, including a TASK.md requirements suite and a content audit (REQUIREMENTS.md maps each TASK.md line to its checks)\\\",\",\"     \\\"research\\\": \\\"None on the web. Read the engine handoff (API notes and the renderer, body, input and dialog source) and the AI Hub lib/hub README, session.js and harness\\\",\",\"     \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\",\",\"     \\\"model\\\": \\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\",\"-    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Cost unknown; tokens unknown; session time about 3 hours (2026-11-03 21:55 to about 2026-11-04 00:55, wall clock)\\\"\",\"+    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Cost unknown; tokens unknown; session time about 3 hours 20 minutes (2026-11-03 21:55 to about 2026-11-04 01:15, wall clock)\\\"\",\"   },\",\"   \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\",\"-    \\\"40, listed in DEVLOG.md: 21 caught by the scripted tests (headless suites, the network suite and the browser checks), 14 by screenshot review (HUD panels overlapping, the quest tracker covering the health bar, clipped prompt rows, tabs past the screen edge), 1 by reading code after a screenshot (Enter both turning and skipping the prologue), and 4 by scans for stubs (a Bee scoring hook that did nothing, a landing squash never drawn, cutscene skips that left a training dummy or skipped a note, Dev rows with empty actions).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"43, listed in DEVLOG.md: 21 caught by the scripted tests (headless suites, the network suite and the browser checks), 14 by screenshot review (HUD panels overlapping, the quest tracker covering the health bar, clipped prompt rows, tabs past the screen edge), 1 by reading code after a screenshot (Enter both turning and skipping the prologue), 4 by scans for stubs (a Bee scoring hook that did nothing, a landing squash never drawn, cutscene skips that left a training dummy or skipped a note, Dev rows with empty actions), and 3 by a content audit that requires everything defined to be used (a Golden Thimble with no effect, a jingle never played, a rock decoration never placed).\\\",\",\"     \\\"7: the game failing to boot from a module load-order error, the residents' path walker recursing until the stack overflowed (a freeze), the quest system never being wired so the story could not advance, a Cheer bubble that could be collected forever, the host's own edits never reaching other players (a desync in multiplayer), the Builder hidden behind walls in the first region by the x-ray and cutaway, and a late regression where a quiet quest completion broke the boot (caught by the next test run).\\\",\",\"-    \\\"The scripted playthrough: an AI pilot plays Chapter One from the first quest to the credits and the side quests through the same input intents a player uses. It found the unwired quests, the path walker freeze, room detection gaps, dialogs blocking play, and story beats that left furniture blocked by plants.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"The scripted playthrough: an AI pilot plays Chapter One from the first quest to the credits and the side quests through the same input intents a player uses. It found the unwired quests, the path walker freeze, room detection gaps, dialogs blocking play, and story beats that left furniture blocked by plants. The content audit came second: it proves nothing defined is unused, and plants a probe of each kind to show it would catch one.\\\",\",\"     \\\"Early unit checks of screen picking and stair heights: their failures were mostly wrong expectations in the tests themselves, not bugs in the game, and the playthrough covered the same code better.\\\"\",\"   ],\",\"   \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":0,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521/DEVLOG.md\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/exit-interview.json\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_0156jJwrn6YbH8kfg7QHjP2q\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghZ6rnn6panqojvdaLx8\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Rebuilding the release so the About screen carries the updated answers, then the full suite one last time.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1416,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":254367,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1416},\"output_tokens\":48,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9acc64b9-af41-4198-9bbd-536ec13fbed1\",\"uuid\":\"51850abb-cdb3-45f9-bae8-600701527519\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T08:14:39.023Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghZ6rTvupykhVKyhUb15\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghZ6rnn6panqojvdaLx8\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01NchcGAK4BTZEDtCWAU1v3m\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"node tools/build.mjs --release | tail -1 && timeout 900 node tests/run.mjs --browser 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-400; cd .. && node -e \\\"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'));console.log('json ok')\\\" && ls -la DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-21